         ByPass Idle Time
         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
         This is to bypass the node's idle timeout setting that kicks users
         off the bbs if they don't do anything in so many minutes.

         This setting can be set higher or lower than the node's setting to
         kick certain users off sooner or let them stay on longer than they
         would of normally.  leave this set to zero if you want the user to
         be kicked with the node's idle timeout setting.

         Keep in mind a long distance caller when adjusting this.  If you set
         a user higher than normal that is calling long distance and they walk
         away from their machine, they will stay on longer before being kicked.
         This will give them a higher phone bill for being on longer, so just
         think about it before you set this setting.


    2.10  TempS (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to give a user temporary sysop
    access.
    - Confirm requester will come up if Confirm is turned on.


    2.11  Abort (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to abort a user's transfer.
    - Confirm requester will come up if Confirm is turned on.


    2.12  Dump (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to kick a user off the bbs.
    - Confirm requester will come up if Confirm is turned on.


    2.13  Bank Cycle (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Sysops can toggle the bottom 24 gadgets to other banks of gadgets.
    These other banks will be sysop defineable banks.
    (Currently not installed).


    2.14  Sysop Login (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to sysop login to the node.


    2.15  Local Login (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to local login on a user's account.


    2.16  Give Carrier (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to give a carrier to a user, so they
    can connect to the BBS from voice.


    2.17  Reserve Node (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to reserve a node for a caller.
    You can enter either user id/slot number or user handle.


    2.18  Un/Iconify (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Select a node, then select this gadget to iconify/un-iconify a node.


    2.19  Un/Protect (Gadget)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    To protect, click gadget and enter a password.  This will lock out all
    gadgets from functioning except for the un/protect gadget.

    To unprotect the server again, click the un/protect gadget and enter the
    same password in.  Then the server will work like before.

    Once you unprotect the server, it remains unprotected until you re-protect
    it again with a password like before.


